e 231): pthread_sigmask's mask is kept by the module, so a mask"] [158 1 "// inherited (posix_spawn's setsigmask, a parent's blocked signal) starts it, as a C process starts with it; the kernel"] [159 1 "// keeps such a signal pending, as Go's threads inherit the mask too."] [172 1 "// writeInterruptible is os.write's write to a blocking pipe, as write(2) is under CPython's handlers (no SA_RESTART: a"] [173 1 "// signal interrupts it, os.write's PyErr_CheckSignals runs the handlers, PEP 475's retry; py-mods-1122, test_io's"] [174 1 "// SignalsTest.test_interrupted_write_*, which hung): in the main thread, a FIFO's write (a regular file's never blocks;"] [175 1 "// sockets write by socket's own calls) waits for room by ppoll with the wake pipe (the GIL released, the handlers run when"] [176 1 "// a signal arrives) and writes at most PIPE_BUF bytes at a time, which a pipe that polls writable takes without blocking"] [177 1 "// (no flag of the shared file description changed), until every byte is written; a handler that raises ends it with its"] [178 1 "// exception (CPython's partial count, then the handler's exception at the next check), one that returns lets it go on."] [179 1 "// handled false: not such a write (another thread, a non-blocking descriptor, no FIFO, nothing to write), written as"] [180 1 "// before."] [193 28 "// the wake pipe made for a write that may wait, not before (readInterruptible's)"] [196 23 "// PIPE_BUF: a pipe that polls writable has at least this much room"]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[97 40] [103 39] [115 33] [127 48] [146 35] [162 91] [165 12] [165 22] [201 35]]} (go/file "builtins_signal_wait.go" :build ["//go:build linux"] :imports [


